Description: parallel best-first search in C++20: A* and branch-and-bound
 PBeFS is a C++20 library for the sequential and parallel best-first
 search of an implicit state-space graph (A*) and of a tree with an
 incumbent (branch-and-bound): the parallel A* searches of the survey of
 Fukunaga et al. (HDA* with its work distributions, SPA*, SafePBNF, PA*SE
 and a master-worker farm) and the parallel branch-and-bound searches
 (shared and distributed queues, work stealing, deterministic rounds and
 SelfSplit), on C++ threads and OpenMP, built on the data structures and
 the executors of ADS.
 .
 This package installs the headers, the static library, the CMake package
 PBeFS (targets PBeFS::PBeFS and PBeFS::OpenMP) and the pkg-config file
 pbefs.pc; the runtimes of FastFlow and MPI are left out.
